WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:11.769
Gooooood

00:00:11.769 --> 00:00:13.960
morning, John, it's Tuesdaaaaaay!

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.940
June 19th.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.700
[singing] I'm back in the basement agaaaain.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.460
I'm back in the basement again!

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:26.640
I'm mostly underground, and you can't hear a sound 'cause I'm back in the basement again!

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.620
It's comfortable here.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.940
I made a little nest for myself

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.000
where I can nuzzle up

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.160
and come down here when it's too hot outside,

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.080
and I'm back in the basement again!

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.620
But, I don't envy you having to move out of your house,

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.740
having to leave your little studio.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.420
I wonder what's gonna be in the background of your new videos?

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.780
Is it still gonna be your bookcase?

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.360
Or are you gonna do it somewhere else?

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.340
Maybe Brotherhood 2.0 viewers would like a change of setting every once in a while.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.620
I mean, for a while, people were, you know,

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.760
impressed by my map of the realm of Narnia

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.140
and my floating bookshelves back there.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.380
But now nobody talks about that anymore.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:04.060
Maybe I should start filming upstairs

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:05.180
in my bedroom

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.060
with the cat

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.540
at the Missoula Skate park

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.520
maybe somewhere from downtown Missoula

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:10.860
Or from Target

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:12.400
You know, on location.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.380
Not today though.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.400
But I'd be interested if people have suggestions.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.940
So what's the news, you ask?

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:19.540
Oh, let me tell you: there's news.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:21.720
There's this news

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.047
You might not be impressed with this kind of stuff John anymore,

00:01:24.047 --> 00:01:25.600
But it's still very exciting for me.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.540
I can go to Barnes and Noble and be like,

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.180
"Hey. I wrote this. That's me."

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:33.440
People will gasp, "You're famous!"

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:34.720
Just like that:

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:35.780
"Famous!"

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:36.960
And I'll say,

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.540
"You don't know the half of it."

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.500
The other day, I was wearing my Brotherhood 2.0

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.470
In my pants shirt, and that lady came up and asked me about it.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.640
I thought that was actually kind of brave of her?

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.720
I mean, would you go up to somebody who had a t-shirt like that?

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.789
I mean, I've seen a lot of weird t-shirts in my time

00:01:50.789 --> 00:01:53.140
but I don't generally walk up to people ask them what they're about.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:54.920
There's an idea for a project!

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.040
Asking people about their t-shirts

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.040
Gotta find someplace public with lots of t-shirts and be like,

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.620
"What the..."

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:06.900
"It's the future! He saw it, and it's going to crush him."

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.300
A lot of times, there's no explaining.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.540
I mean, talking to strangers is fun right?

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.340
As long as the t-shirt doesn't say something like

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.640
"Don't talk to me about mah t-shirt

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.240
or I will put forks in you!"

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.020
That would be an amazing t-shirt!

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.040
Other news!

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.760
I was on the Weather Channel!

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.800
I mean, I knew that they had recorded me for the Weather Channel

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:27.160
but then suddenly, I was actually ON the Weather Channel.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:30.520
I missed it, but it will be on again several times.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.680
The show is called "Forecast Earth"

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:33.720
I believe

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.500
The particular episode is entitled

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.940
Something about

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:38.540
hotness

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:39.420
heat

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.460
global heat

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.280
heating up

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.680
heater or heaters

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:43.980
space heater

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.040
Space heater? Probably not.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.640
It starts out, I think with John Kerry

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.240
and I'm at the very end.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.060
But that's definitely my first national television appearance.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.120
And I'm pretty sure that they mentioned Brotherhood 2.0!

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.000
Woo party Hank woo Hank party!

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.019
Anyhow, I talked to The Yeti this afternoon

00:02:58.019 --> 00:03:00.300
And she and John were in the moving truck

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.580
leaving New York!

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.120
Actually, trying to get out of the city while in a moving truck.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.680
Which I'm sure can't be very easy.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.020
So, let us all get together

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.940
And say lucky, lucky, lucky, lucky, lucky, lucky woo!

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.040
Good luck getting out of the city and getting to Indianapolis!

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.760
Good luck moving into your new house!

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.060
Good luck doing a video tomorrow!

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.840
while moving into your new house

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.040
cause that's gonna suck.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.880
And thanks for your video. It always sucks leaving a good place.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.420
I hope I don't have to do it anytime soon.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:29.760
I'll see you tomorrow. I hope.

